            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for a victim, then the Hindi for refuge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: बिछुड़ना",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बिछुड़ना — bichuṛnā — \"to be separated\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मेले में एक बच्चा अपनी माँ से बिछुड़ गया। mele meṁ ek baccā apnī māṁ se bichuṛ gayā. At the fair a child got separated from his mother."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): वह बच्चा बिछुड़ गया, vah baccā bichuṛ gayā."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बिछुड़ना (bichuṛnā) is inherited from vikṣuṭati, a form CDIAL reconstructs (CDIAL 11651). The one you are parted from takes से: माँ से बिछुड़ गया."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
